{"name":"Loggia Lights","hex":"#e1ebde","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"loggia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A roofed, open gallery, usually on an upper level."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loggia"},{"term":"lights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of light"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The lungs, now chiefly of an animal (being lighter than adjacent parts)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loggia","blocks":[{"text":"In architecture, a loggia is a covered exterior gallery or corridor, often on an upper level, sometimes on the ground level of a building. The corridor is open to the elements because its outer wall is only partial, with the upper part usually supported by a series of columns or arches. An overhanging loggia may be supported by a baldresca."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ratusz2007.jpg/330px-Ratusz2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loggia","wikidata":"Q466544"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg/500px-Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg/1280px-Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg/500px-Palladio_Villa_Godi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Villa Godi by Palladio. The portico is the focal point in the center with loggias used at each side of the structure as a corridor.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APalladio_Villa_Godi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4